3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\nWrong attempts used: 2/8. Demo requests used: 4/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find the repeated lattice spacing from rows/columns that are mostly\n    # horizontal/vertical grid lines (rather than the uniform tile interiors).\n    row_scores = [sum(v != grid[0][0] for v in row) for row in grid]\n    line_rows = [r for r, score in enumerate(row_scores) if score >= 2]\n    col_scores = [sum(grid[r][c] != grid[0][0] for r in range(h)) for c in range(w)]\n    line_cols = [c for c, score in enumerate(col_scores) if score >= 2]\n\n    # In these patterns the lattice intersections are spaced regularly.\n    def regular_positions(pos):\n        if len(pos) < 2:\n            return pos\n        step = min(b-a for a, b in zip(pos, pos[1:]) if b > a)\n        return [p for p in pos if (p-pos[0]) % step == 0]\n\n    rr = regular_positions(line_rows)\n    cc = regular_positions(line_cols)\n    if len(rr) > 1:\n        rr = rr[:-1]\n    if len(cc) > 1:\n        cc = cc[:-1]\n\n    # The common color at lattice intersections is the line color; replace it\n    # with the ordinary tile fill color, while preserving encoded markers.\n    counts = {}\n    for row in grid:\n        for v in row:\n            counts[v] = counts.get(v, 0) + 1\n    line_color = max(counts, key=counts.get)\n    fill = next((v for v in counts if v != line_color and v not in (4, 6)), line_color)\n\n    return [[fill if grid[r][c] == line_color else grid[r][c] for c in cc] for r in rr]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct